{"step_index":262,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T19:45:04Z","thinking":"**Diagnosing Search Scope Limitation**\n\nThe search is constrained by the selected area filter (\"Mirpur, Dhaka\"). Typing \"medcare\" searches within that scope. The expected result, \"MedCare Pharmacy\", is in \"Dhanmondi\", a different area.\n\n\n**Refining Search Logic for Usability**\n\nThe current `AND` search condition with area filtering leads to no results when the pharmacy isn't in the selected area. Users likely expect to find pharmacies by name regardless of the area. A more flexible approach would prioritize a pharmacy name search across all areas, and if no match is found within the chosen area, expand the search to all areas, displaying a notification of the change. Expanding the area coverage of popular pharmacy chains would also enhance search accuracy.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\medcheck-bd\\server\\routes\\pharmacies.js","EndLine":65,"StartLine":15,"toolAction":"View pharmacies search route","toolSummary":"View pharmacies.js query logic"}}]}
