ry (`pharmacies.html`) returned \"No Pharmacies Found\".\n  - Screenshots showed:\n    1. Area: `Mirpur, Dhaka` | Medicine: `seclo` | Pharmacy: `medcare` -> *No Pharmacies Found*\n    2. Area: `Mirpur, Dhaka` | Medicine: `napa` | Pharmacy: `lazz pharma` -> *No Pharmacies Found*\n- **Root Cause Identified**:\n  - `MedCare Pharmacy` and `Lazz Pharma` in `seedData.js` were originally seeded only in `Dhanmondi, Dhaka`. In `Mirpur`, the seeded pharmacy was `Tamanna Pharmacy Mirpur`.\n  - When the user selected \"Mirpur, Dhaka\" and typed \"medcare\" or \"lazz pharma\", `server/routes/pharmacies.js` performed a strict SQL-style `AND` (`{ area: 'Mirpur', name: /medcare/i }`), returning 0 results because MedCare is in Dhanmondi, not Mirpur.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress & Current State\n- **Project Path**: `C:\\Users\\User\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\medcheck-bd`\n- **Application Server**: Node.js/Express running on `http://localhost:5000` (task `task-220`).\n- **Database**: Local MongoDB (`mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017/medcheck_bd`) with 67+ medicines, 137 batches, and 200+ inventory records.\n- **Completed Improvements**:\n  - `server/routes/medicines.js`: Added `/api/medicines/suggestions` autocomplete endpoint.\n  - `server/routes/verify.js`: Smart tokenized search (handles `napa500`, `seclo20`, unit stripping like `mg/ml`, fuzzy generic and brand matching). Returns alternative suggestions if no match.\n  - `server/routes/inventory.js`: Upgraded `/api/inventory/compare` with tokenized matching.\n  - `client/css/style.css`: Added `.autocomplete-dropdown` and `.autocomplete-item` styling.\n  - `client/js/main.js`: Added `setupMedicineAutocomplete(inputId, onSelectCallback)`.\n  - `client/js/verify.js`: Connected autocomplete to `verifyInput` and enhanced `renderNotFoundResult` with suggested medicines.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings\n- In `pharmacies.html`, users expect that:\n  1. Popular pharmacy chains like `Lazz Pharma` and `MedCare Pharmacy` exist in `Mirpur` as well as `Dhanmondi` and `Uttara`.\n  2. If an area filter like `Mirpur` is selected, but the user searches for a specific pharmacy name located in another area (like `MedCare` in `Dhanmondi`), the system shouldn't silently fail; it should either relax the area filter or notify the user that MedCare was found in Dhanmondi.\n  3. Search inputs on `pharmacies.html` (`filterMedicine` and `searchPharmacy`) previously only triggered on `Enter` keyup, not live typing.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Active Context\n- Background task `task-220` is running `node server/server.js`.\n- Files pending updates:\n  - `server/routes/pharmacies.js`: Needs smart fallback when `area` + `search` yields 0 results.\n  - `server/seed/seedData.js`: Needs `Lazz Pharma Mirpur` and `MedCare Pharmacy Mirpur` added to the pharmacies list with stock.\n  - `client/js/pharmacy.js` & `client/pharmacies.html`: Needs debounced live search (`input` listener) and fallback banner handling.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Next Steps (In Priority Order)\n1. **Update `server/seed/seedData.js`**:\n   - Add Mirpur branches for `Lazz Pharma` and `MedCare Pharmacy` (e.g. `Lazz Pharma Mirpur`, `MedCare Pharmacy Mirpur`) with active stock for `Napa`, `Seclo`, etc.\n   - Run `node server/seed/seedData.js` to seed the new branches.\n2. **Update `server/routes/pharmacies.js`**:\n   - In `GET /api/pharmacies`, if `area && search` returns 0 matches, perform a relaxed search across all areas. Return matches with `fallbackToAllAreas: true` and `matchedArea: p.area`.\n3. **Update `client/js/pharmacy.js` & `client/pharmacies.html`**:\n   - Add debounced live typing on `searchPharmacy` and `filterMedicine`.\n   - When `data.fallbackToAllAreas` is true, render a friendly banner: *\"No branch found specifically in Mirpur, but found [X] matching pharmacies in Dhanmondi.\"*\n   - Add `setupMedicineAutocomplete` on `filterMedicine`.\n4. **Restart Server**:\n   - Kill daemon `task-220` and restart `node server/server.js`.\n5. **Verify & Respond**:\n   - Test `http:/